.TH S3M-VER 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-ver \- object version and delete-marker manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-ver
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fBs3://\fIBUCKET\fR[\fB/\fIPREFIX\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists and manages object versions and delete markers.
With no pruning options it lists every stored version as CSV.
With pruning options it is a \fBdry run\fR listing what would be deleted; add \fB\-\-apply\fR to delete.
.SH PRUNING OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-keep " N"
Per key, keep the newest N non-current versions (in addition to the current version) and delete the rest.
\fB\-\-keep 0\fR keeps only the current version.
.TP
.BI \-\-older\-than " DUR"
Only delete versions older than DUR (\fB30d\fR, \fB12h\fR, \fB45m\fR, \fB4w\fR).
Combined with \fB\-\-keep\fR, a version must fail both tests to be deleted.
.TP
.B \-\-markers
Also delete a key's delete markers when the key is left with no versions at all (tombstone cleanup).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-markers
Delete nothing but delete markers.
Removing a latest marker undeletes the object.
.TP
.B \-\-latest
Allow \fB\-\-older\-than\fR to delete the current version too; the previous version becomes current.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually delete.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the CSV to FILE and show live progress.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-rm (1),
.BR s3m\-find (1)
